---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../config/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="An informal association working to connect Revillagigedo Island's trails across jurisdictions."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-tide">About</p>
    <h1 class="font-display mt-2 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">{site.name}</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed">
      Working name for the Ketchikan Trail Association — an informal group of residents who want
      the island's trails to function as a network. There is no entity and no 501(c)(3). That is
      why this site does not ask for money.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold">Who this is for</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 leading-relaxed">
      <li>Residents who already use the trails and can see the gaps between them.</li>
      <li>
        Land managers — USFS, State, Mental Health Trust, Borough, City, Native corporations —
        who need a coherent, honest plan that spans jurisdictions.
      </li>
      <li>Future funders who need a mapped project pipeline, not a brochure.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold">Partners we have to talk to</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      Tongass National Forest, Alaska State Parks, the Alaska Mental Health Trust, Ketchikan
      Gateway Borough, the City of Ketchikan, the City of Saxman, and Native corporations with
      surface estate on Revilla. None of them are listed here as endorsing the map.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold">Board</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      Names go here when the group is ready to put them on a public page. Until then, write
      {" "}
      <a class="underline decoration-contour underline-offset-4" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold">Legal posture</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      This is not legal advice. The group should get some before taking a dollar. The two ordinary
      paths are incorporating as an Alaska nonprofit with DCCED and filing IRS Form 1023-EZ, or
      operating under a fiscal sponsor — Alaska Trails or a community foundation — and taking
      donations through them in the meantime.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
